.TH OBS-LIVESTREAM 1 2026-10-28 "just3ws" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
obs-livestream \- manage, validate, and broadcast UGtastic oral history rewatch livestreams
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bundle exec rake validate:obs
.br
.B ruby bin/validate_obs_setup.rb
[\fB\-\-live\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.br
.B obs/scripts/install-obs-config.sh
[\fB\-\-dry-run\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.br
.B obs/scripts/update-overlay-state.sh
[\fB\-\-episode\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-guest\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-conference\fR \fICONF\fR] [\fB\-\-prompt\fR \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-\-help\fR]
.br
.B obs/scripts/test-audio-routing.sh
[\fB\-\-help\fR]
.br
.B bin/broadcast --playbook
.br
.B bin/broadcast --preflight
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B obs-livestream
is the automation and configuration suite for the "The Sound Above" oral history rewatch stream. Hosted by Mike Hall (UGtastic Creator), the series reviews over 200 UGtastic interviews (2010\[en]2015), early Chicago software craftsmanship history, and the evolution of developer identity as the industry transitions into the AI era.
.PP
The toolchain provides declarative OBS Studio 33 scene collections, Apple Silicon VideoToolbox hardware encoding profiles, native macOS ScreenCaptureKit and CoreAudio capture, interactive browser overlays, a recording-day dashboard, and automated local contract checks.
.SH PRODUCTION SCENES
The scene collection defines eight purpose-built broadcast scenes:
.TP
.B 01. Starting Soon
Ambient slate title screen with live episode card, quote carousel, and animated pulse indicator.
.TP
.B 02. Monologue / Full Camera
Full-screen host camera with lower-third HUD for framing historical context and opening thesis.
.TP
.B 03. Reaction \- Video Focus
Full-frame Chromium interview with a 480x270 host camera inset at the lower right, Now Watching HUD, and isolated application audio.
.TP
.B 04. Split Screen \- Video & Research
Side-by-side comparison: Chromium video playback on the left, secondary research browser or terminal on the right showing transcripts or timeline data on just3ws.localhost.
.TP
.B 05. Workbench \- Code & Terminal
Full-screen terminal window capture (18pt font minimum) with host camera inset for code analysis, git archaeology, and zdots platform tooling demonstrations.
.TP
.B 06. Guest & Co-Host Discussion
Two-up side-by-side camera boxes with shared screen inset for retrospective discussions with community veterans.
.TP
.B 07. Intermission / BRB
Standby card ("Holding the Thread") displaying the active topic while stepping away from the workbench.
.TP
.B 08. Outro & Next Stream
Closing credits, archive resource links, and next episode preview.
.SH AUDIO ARCHITECTURE (MACOS GOLDEN GATE)
OBS on macOS Golden Gate (Darwin 27) utilizes native ScreenCaptureKit and CoreAudio capture:
.IP \(bu 2
.B Per-Application Audio (\fIsck_audio_capture\fR):
Taps the digital PCM stream of the Chromium browser directly. Completely isolates video playback while automatically filtering out Mail chimes, Slack dings, terminal bells, and Spotify.
.IP \(bu 2
.B Desktop Audio (\fIcoreaudio_output_capture\fR):
Configured but disabled in the rewatch scene collection to prevent duplicate Chromium playback and system notification sounds. Enable only for a deliberately designed session that needs system-wide audio.
.IP \(bu 2
.B 4-Track Master Recording:
Advanced recording captures four synchronized tracks in one hybrid MOV per session. Automatic time and size splitting are disabled. Track 1 is the host mic plus Chromium program mix at 320 kbps AAC; Track 2 is the isolated host mic; Track 3 is isolated Chromium audio; Track 4 is reserved and unassigned.
.SH OVERLAYS
Browser overlays in \fIobs/overlays/\fR poll \fIobs/overlays/overlay-state.json\fR every 2.5 seconds:
.TP
.B lower-third.html
Renders interviewee name, event, year, role, and the central Sound Above philosophical prompt.
.TP
.B now-watching.html
Renders floating metadata card with recording indicator, era pill, and episode topic.
.TP
.B stream-starting.html
Pre-stream title card with animated pulse and rotating quotes from craftsmanship literature.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I obs/scenes/ugtastic-sound-above.json
Declarative OBS Studio 33 scene collection.
.TP
.I docs/recording-playbook.md
Canonical preparation, local test, recording, streaming, recovery, and close procedure.
.TP
.I obs/profiles/The Sound Above/basic.ini
OBS profile for Apple Silicon VideoToolbox capture and multitrack recording.
.TP
.I obs/overlays/overlay-state.json
Live state synchronized to browser sources.
.TP
.I obs/curation/sequence-manifest.json
37-episode master curation sequence (35 interview episodes plus 2 codas).
.TP
.I obs/curation/errata-manifest.json
Curated catalog for Errata readings, concepts, live demos, and artifacts.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Application Support/obs-studio/
Installed OBS Studio configuration target.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Direct broadcasts via unified CLI:
bin/broadcast --status
bin/broadcast --rewatch 1
bin/broadcast --errata --cue errata-concept-blink-test

# Validate all OBS contracts and macOS environment:
bundle exec rake validate:obs

# Probe running OBS instance and WebSocket socket:
ruby bin/validate_obs_setup.rb --live

# Synchronize repo configuration to OBS Studio:
# OBS must be closed before installation.
\&./obs/scripts/install-obs-config.sh --dry-run
\&./obs/scripts/install-obs-config.sh

# Print the end-to-end recording and streaming playbook:
bin/broadcast --playbook

# Run local repository and environment preflight checks:
bin/broadcast --preflight

# Run audio diagnostic and sample rate check:
\&./obs/scripts/test-audio-routing.sh
.fi
